WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:29.080
Even Summoned Skull can't destroy Zera.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.740
There's no way I can destroy that ultra rare card!

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.180
Come out, the other Yugi.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.510
What should I do?

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:49.890
Millennium Puzzle in Pieces

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.880
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.420
Stay calm.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.520
Keith is acting strange.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.970
He's relying on rare cards instead of his Machine deck.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:25.260
Since he's lost sight of his tactics, he now has weaknesses.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.130
I place a monster in defense position.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.640
An array of rare cards and traps are pressuring him.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:53.660
The soul inside the Millennium Puzzle will have to come out.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.160
Seiyaryu.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.670
And one more card.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.820
The ultra rare Magic Jammer.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:22.670
And the spell card Stop Defense!

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.790
Koumori Dragon!

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.930
I switched your Koumori Dragon to attack position.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.530
Zera the Mant, Devil's Claw!

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:44.040
Koumori Dragon is destroyed!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.240
Come out, the other Yugi.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.780
Are you the man I think you are?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.780
Don't come out, my other self.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.350
I can manage this on my own.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.440
Stop Defense ends this turn!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:06.820
My turn!

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.300
I place a monster in defense position!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.600
Seiyaryu attacks the defending monster.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.540
Holy Flame!

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.810
I set two more cards on the field.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.840
I switch Zera the Mant to defense position.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.720
I end my turn.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.760
It's your turn.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.440
You don't have any monsters on your field.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.490
What will you do?

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.040
I set one card.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.000
I summon Dark Magician!

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:54.740
And I use the spell card Magical Hats!

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.260
That's your signature move.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.480
I'll use a spell card.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.820
I activate Magic Jammer.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:17.340
By discarding one card from my hand, the rare card Magic Jammer negates and destroys your spell card.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.610
No!  Magical Hats!

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:36.200
The spell card Curse of Fiend switches the battle positions of all monsters on the field.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.420
And monsters can't change battle position this turn.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.620
This card can only be used during the Standby Phase.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.590
Zera the Mant battles Dark Magician.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.360
Devil's Claw!

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.730
Now's my chance!  Mirror Force!

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.970
I activate the trap card Solemn Judgment.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.820
No way!

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.980
Solemn Judgment is an ultra rare card!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:21.390
By paying half my life points, this card negates and destroys a spell, trap or monster summoning.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:31.800
My life points are halved to 250, but you only have 100 life points.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.960
You're on the edge of defeat.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:08.020
I promised my other self that I'd get the Millennium Puzzle back.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.810
The battle isn't over yet.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.810
I can't give up before I lose!

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:16.280
A miracle will happen.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.260
No, I'll make a miracle happen!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:20.820
Good!

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:23.050
I set a card on the field.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.360
I place a monster in defense position.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.780
He's still trying instead of giving up.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.710
Come out, the other person hiding inside the Millennium Puzzle!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.210
I'll use this card to pull him out of the vessel.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.160
Tribute to The Doomed.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.660
Tribute to The Doomed?

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.530
Another ultra rare card!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:54.180
Yes.  It's the spell card among spell cards.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:08:00.700
With Tribute to The Doomed, I discard a card from my hand to destroy a monster on the field.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.220
This is the finishing blow.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.770
Are you sure about that?

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:10.800
That's...

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:15.810
Spell Shattering Arrow switches your spell's target from my monster to yours.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.540
I target Zera the Mant!

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:28.720
What?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:44.100
Someone is controlling Bandit Keith.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.010
The Millennium Ring's power will sever that bond!

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:02.020
What was that impact?

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:04.080
It was shadow power.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.480
There's someone there besides Yugi.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.030
What have I been doing?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:16.620
You ignored your own deck and relied on ultra rare cards that were given to you.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.150
Your pride will be your downfall!

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.540
You can't stop my momentum!

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.710
You're Yugi!

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:25.220
Why are you here?

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.850
Keith?

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:28.710
What's wrong?

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:32.730
Keith, you're under my control again.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.720
You must fight until you bring the other Yugi out of the Millennium Puzzle.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.860
Millennium Puzzle?

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.530
Who's giving me orders?

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:44.820
What?

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.600
Don't enter my mind!

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:51.100
Is this what my other self was talking about?

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:54.320
You have to fight this duel on your own!

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.130
But why?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.080
I have a bad feeling.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.340
I feel like someone is watching me.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:05.110
Someone is controlling Keith!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:11.340
Bandit Keith, you are my servant and under my control!

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:16.540
No!  Stop it!

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:23.130
Not until you find out the identity of the soul inside the Millennium Puzzle.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.340
It's all the fault of this thing!

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.010
No!  Don't do it, Keith!

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:00.960
Keith!

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.240
Please stop!

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.750
Stop it!

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.510
Yugi!

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:20.970
Bakura!

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.560
Yugi, Anzu told me what happened.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.800
It's your duty to rebuild this.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:34.020
That's what the Puzzle wants.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.800
Yeah.  Thank you.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:41.550
But it takes a long time to complete the Millennium Puzzle.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:45.620
It took me eight years the first time.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:49.600
I don't know when we'll meet again.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:54.270
But I promise to rebuild it, even if takes me decades.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:07.950
I'll now execute the real reason I came here.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:15.170
Yugi, you don't know the true power hidden inside the Millennium Puzzle.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:18.500
The other Yugi doesn't either.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:25.880
The Millennium Puzzle contains the memories of an ancient Pharaoh from 3000 years ago.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:33.660
When the other six Items are gathered, the memories are unsealed and restored.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:39.440
One of the keys is this Millennium Ring.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:45.300
This is what's written in stone at an underground temple at Kul Elna:

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:55.020
"The young Pharaoh and his six priests sacrificed their lives to seal an evil power behind a sacred door."

00:12:55.280 --> 00:13:01.020
"I hope the evil power and the Pharaoh's memories never resurrect."

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:08.320
If I can find the Pharaoh's memories inside the Millennium Puzzle, I can acquire the evil power.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:17.400
The Millennium Ring has the power to put a part of my soul inside an object, such as this Puzzle piece!

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.050
Parasite Mind!

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.050
It's done.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:31.550
Now I just wait for Yugi to complete the Puzzle.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:38.760
The piece of my soul is a mind spy that secretly enters the Millennium Puzzle's labyrinth of memories.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:43.780
It will find the sacred memories hidden inside the room of truth.

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:45.970
Yugi.

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.520
You forgot one of the Puzzle pieces.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.070
Thank you, Bakura!

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:54.070
The Puzzle can't be completed if even a single piece is missing.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:55.590
Yes.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:58.190
Hey, we have to get to school!

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.320
We're already late!

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.880
Thank you very much, Bakura.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.050
Ouch...

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:05.590
Are you okay?

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:08.460
Yeah.  I'll go on ahead.

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:12.080
Okay.  I'll go when I unhook the Puzzle's chain.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:25.060
Keith...  Wake up, Keith...

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.580
What's wrong?

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:31.160
You still have life points.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.550
You must battle, Keith...

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:36.550
Who are you?

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:42.060
Don't order me around!

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.550
Keith...

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:12.000
Where's Yugi?

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:17.930
That's...

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:18.800
A fire!

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.700
Ahh!  A fire!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.570
I gotta free the Puzzle fast!

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.700
It's no good!  It won't budge!

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.040
The Puzzle is in danger!

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.020
What should I do?

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:43.220
My other self, answer me!

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:45.290
He can't.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:49.870
I can't ditch my other self.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:55.470
If I abandon him and this place burns down, I'll never see my other self again.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:06.380
The arrows stop here.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.740
Is Yugi inside?

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:11.470
Anzu, call 9-1-1!

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:12.680
Will do!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.170
Hot hot hot!

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:33.610
My other self, I'm sorry that your soul broke apart.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:37.150
Just wait.  I promise to complete the Puzzle.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.880
Then we can see each other again.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.140
And I can apologize to you.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.220
Honda, let's do it!

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:45.960
Yeah!

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:49.750
Again!

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:06.000
Just a little more until I can see you again.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.060
Ready, Honda?

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:08.690
Yeah!

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.070
I'll break you down!

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:14.880
Yugi!

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:17.540
What?

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:18.270
Keith?

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.630
Why is he here?

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.160
That punk!

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.570
Wait!  It's more important to find Yugi!

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:27.720
Yeah.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.200
Where are you, Yugi?

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.840
What are you doing, Yugi?

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:38.040
Run away now!

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.670
Honda, Jonouchi!

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.610
I have to complete the Puzzle!

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:44.640
What's that fool talking about?

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:52.520
I did it.

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.120
Hang in there, Yugi!

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:03.280
Is he okay?

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:03.980
I don't know.

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:08.580
I can't leave the Puzzle behind.

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.290
Puzzle?

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.560
It doesn't come off!

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.290
Honda!  Jonouchi!

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.580
Are you still inside?

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:29.200
Found it.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:33.240
His deck is safe.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.500
Let's go right now!

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.080
Yeah...

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.590
He won't let go of the Puzzle.

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:44.000
Honda!  Jonouchi!

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:48.770
We're out of time!

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:49.790
In that case...

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.010
Yugi, let go of the Puzzle!

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.670
Please let go of the Puzzle!

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:58.810
If you stay here, you'll die!

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:00.650
Damn!

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.460
It's no good.  It won't budge.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.270
I won't give up!

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:23.830
Jonouchi, pull out the wedge!

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:25.710
What was that?

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.250
Honda, a lever!

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.400
We'll pull out the wedge with a lever!

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:31.240
Yeah!

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:35.380
Fulcrum, leverage and load point!

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:48.180
There are people inside!

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:49.560
Please save them!

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.060
Yugi!

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:57.090
Don't worry.  He's fine.

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:58.650
Look.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:02.170
He built the Puzzle in the fire.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:07.650
He grabbed and wouldn't let go of his bond.

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:14.890
When I first completed the Millennium Puzzle, it took me eight years.

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:18.560
But this time, I completed it in a short amount of time.

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:24.780
It was like my other self inside the Puzzle was helping me.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.900
Yeah, I can understand that.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.900
What happened, Jonouchi?

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:35.910
I think I heard the other Yugi's voice back then.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:37.470
It makes sense.

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:41.150
Your plan was too good for a dummy like you.

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:42.680
What?

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.060
You know I'm right!

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:45.110
What!

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.570
No fighting in the hospital!

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:49.150
Oops, sorry.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:52.590
Anyway, I wasn't sure how it was going to turn out.

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:55.160
Thank you.  You two saved my life.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:56.300
It's fine.

00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:58.160
You don't need to thank us.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.180
I'll go buy some drinks.

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:17.420
I thought the other Yugi was his alter ego, and the Millennium Puzzle triggered him to appear.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.420
That's what I believed and hoped.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.000
But...

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:31.340
Is the other Yugi a completely different person who lives inside the Puzzle?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.180
An exhibition on ancient Egypt will open at Domino Museum.

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:49.260
Ishizu Ishtar of the Egypt Archaeological Society arrives, and something important will be exhibited.

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:52.500
But why is Kaiba meeting her?

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:55.260
Ancient duels?  God Cards?

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:58.640
Something is about to begin in Domino City.

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:01.800
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Pharaoh's Lost Memories

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:03.380
Duel, standby!

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:21.760
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:27.130
I feel like I've been here

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:36.810
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:37.110 --> 00:22:48.320
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:55.830
Time passes bit by bit

00:22:56.500 --> 00:23:01.100
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:06.210
Will never change

00:23:06.870 --> 00:23:11.480
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:12.110 --> 00:23:16.680
To be who I am

00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:21.920
I've kept searching for something

00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:26.630
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:29.560
I learned that's the answer

00:23:30.360 --> 00:23:36.670
From now until forever...
